 ## Overview
-The Volume Raycasting Pipeline is the standard procedural framework for direct volume rendering, calculating the volume rendering integral for every viewing ray originating at the image plane and passing through the volume [S1, unofficial]. It advances rays through the volume with regular increments, performing reconstruction, classification, shading, and compositing at each sample location [S1, unofficial]. It is distinguished from its siblings by its explicit separation of these four stages and the critical decision of whether classification and shading occur before or after reconstruction (pre- vs. post-), where post-classification and post-shading are preferred to avoid severe artifacts caused by non-linear reconstruction [S1, unofficial].
